Title: SDL3: minimum window size; never create an empty surface
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-18
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: A window shrunk until its client area divided by the UI scale is 0 makes SDL3Display::recreateSurface() ask SDL_CreateSurface for an empty surface; the "Failed to create surface" exception ends the program and unsaved work is lost. Seen on AROS One after fast resizing down to a 32 pixel wide window.
Change: The surface size is at least 1x1. The window also asks SDL for a minimum size of 320x240; the AROS SDL backend does not apply a minimum set after the window opened (measured: the window still shrank to 32 px), so on AROS only the clamp takes effect.
Scope: SDL3 backend, all platforms
Upstream: candidate (LibreSprite)
Verification: builds for x86_64 ABIv11, mainline x86_64 and Raspberry Pi without warnings. The crash case itself was not re-run after the change.
Removal: when upstream sets a minimum size and checks the surface size.
---
diff --git a/src/she/sdl3/sdl3_display.cpp b/src/she/sdl3/sdl3_display.cpp
index a63b4585ccf1b1070a4283d0ca0721df2d529251..b59c075b271415f60a7b6bf4ed59e8bf176dcd68 100644
--- a/src/she/sdl3/sdl3_display.cpp
+++ b/src/she/sdl3/sdl3_display.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 
 #include <SDL3/SDL.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <sstream>
 #include <iostream>
@@ -62,6 +63,11 @@ namespace she {
       if (!m_window)
 	      throw DisplayCreationException(SDL_GetError());
 
+      // A window shrunk to almost nothing leaves no room for the UI, and a
+      // client area of 0 pixels makes recreateSurface() fail and end the
+      // program. Keep the window usable.
+      SDL_SetWindowMinimumSize(m_window, 320, 240);
+
       if (gpu)
 	      m_renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(m_window, nullptr);
 
@@ -167,7 +173,9 @@ namespace she {
   {
     if (!m_scale)
       return;
-    auto  newSurface = new SDL3Surface(width() / m_scale, height() / m_scale, SDL3Surface::DeleteAndDestroy);
+    // Never ask for an empty surface: SDL_CreateSurface fails on 0 and the
+    // exception would end the program in the middle of a resize.
+    auto  newSurface = new SDL3Surface(std::max(1, width() / m_scale), std::max(1, height() / m_scale), SDL3Surface::DeleteAndDestroy);
     if (m_surface) {
       m_surface->blitTo(newSurface, 0, 0, 0, 0, width() / m_scale, height() / m_scale);
       m_surface->dispose();
